# What must never reach the build context.
#
# web/node_modules is the load-bearing line. rollup and esbuild ship
# platform-specific native binaries, this tree is built on Windows and the
# image is Linux, so a copied node_modules does not slow the build down, it
# breaks it. It is also 116 MB of upload on every build.
#
# web/dist is excluded for a different reason: the image builds it. A stale
# dist copied in from a developer's machine would be served as if it were the
# thing the Dockerfile built, and the served interface would not match the
# commit the image reports.
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
tests
video
infra
__pycache__
*.pyc
.venv
.coverage
htmlcov
